Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Abstract", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979218099462522*^9, 
  3.9792181050063763`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3dc080c2-cce6-4817-a2dc-\
6249b340d407"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Kerr metric around a spinning black hole is much more difficult than \
the Schwarzschild. The quest to find and solve its field equations took some \
50 years from Einstein\[CloseCurlyQuote]s publishing of general relativity in \
1915. The ",
 StyleBox["dramatis",
  IgnoreSpellCheck->True,
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 StyleBox[" personae",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " include Boyer, Lindquist, Kerr, Ernst, Chandrasekhar, and others who \
published results from 1965 to 1968. We tell the story not historically, but \
as a fable of challenge and victory, in a spirit of rigorous fun. Along the \
way, we stress-test \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] and the Relativity \
Toolkit, v1.10.0. That\[CloseCurlyQuote]s the novel contribution of this \
notebook."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJxTTMoPSmViYGAQB2IQrcmxcMrBpW8d3VRfgunV0S9mgmi92uuLQXRV93Le
i0B6g/5LYRDN331DAkTf9P2sD6K3qTi4gejXR28Fg+iDKRb5YPEK0zYQXSHb
NBFEC4QHLAHR7/vnXQDRM3XiHoLoHpEk1ktAmmcjrwSI5mLY5QiiDbtsnEC0
yXM/1cdA2stdSB1Ep+zdGguip30PzQDRbZcdqp8Aad53zK0guunJi3MgOknx
I5jWEjKqfQqkZfWap4LoWfu+bQTR5+YEbQPRcttkdoHoXakr9oDoeUbnD4Ho
Q8pph0F045JDOs+AtN/9KiMQ7VhvPQlE31v8bDaInhFpdeMFkHZf++0WiJY/
mX72FZA2sDM8B6Kj5vxueg2k6+I3NINoAEDI1fw=
  "],ExpressionUUID->"aafbfaad-d4ad-4821-827b-5be544be948a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Unlike static Schwarzschild, Kerr has off-diagonal terms that couple time \
and rotation: ",
 StyleBox["frame-dragging",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Light cones near the black hole are tipped in the spin direction, \
dragging orbits out of the Keplerian plane. The effect is also called ",
 StyleBox["gravitomagnetism",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", due to its resemblance to electrodynamical magnetism, both producing \
stresses perpendicular to planes of motion. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979218085032246*^9, 3.9792180872858*^9}, {
   3.97921812726119*^9, 3.9792182067340307`*^9}, {3.979249773235776*^9, 
   3.979249823287071*^9}, {3.979249862766975*^9, 3.979250047603253*^9}, {
   3.9792502260044813`*^9, 3.9792503561455803`*^9}, {3.979250406313347*^9, 
   3.979250464214533*^9}, {3.979250526904248*^9, 3.979250529904133*^9}, {
   3.979250806477247*^9, 3.9792508124431543`*^9}, {3.9792512061710463`*^9, 
   3.979251215056979*^9}, {3.9792517417694597`*^9, 3.979251743187923*^9}, {
   3.979286924869732*^9, 3.979287022481254*^9}, {3.979287054116839*^9, 
   3.979287056528462*^9}, {3.9792921521228113`*^9, 3.9792921775299664`*^9}, {
   3.9792922167166653`*^9, 3.9792922857980747`*^9}, {3.979292341083699*^9, 
   3.979292345378234*^9}, {3.9792923794165373`*^9, 3.979292404346846*^9}, {
   3.979292443437128*^9, 3.9792925489681253`*^9}, 3.979293089384967*^9, {
   3.979293937924892*^9, 
   3.9792940974979887`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f34d759b-8e35-4d18-9d65-\
c7e209bb4b38"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Over time, stable Kerr orbits trace out toroidal structures via nodal \
precession similar to that of a Lagrange top. This precession is additional \
to precession of the perihelion, present even in Schwarzschild (non-rotating) \
geometry. Kerr black holes also have ",
 StyleBox["Ergospheres",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", aka ",
 StyleBox["static limits",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", spacetime boundaries outside the event horizons. Inside an Ergosphere, \
spacetime itself flows faster than light. Inflowing geodesics are swept along \
the spinning direction of the black hole."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979218085032246*^9, 3.9792180872858*^9}, {
   3.97921812726119*^9, 3.9792182067340307`*^9}, {3.979249773235776*^9, 
   3.979249823287071*^9}, {3.979249862766975*^9, 3.979250047603253*^9}, {
   3.9792502260044813`*^9, 3.9792503561455803`*^9}, {3.979250406313347*^9, 
   3.979250464214533*^9}, {3.979250526904248*^9, 3.979250529904133*^9}, {
   3.979250806477247*^9, 3.9792508124431543`*^9}, {3.9792512061710463`*^9, 
   3.979251215056979*^9}, {3.9792517417694597`*^9, 3.979251743187923*^9}, {
   3.979286924869732*^9, 3.979287022481254*^9}, {3.979287054116839*^9, 
   3.979287056528462*^9}, {3.9792921521228113`*^9, 3.9792921775299664`*^9}, {
   3.9792922167166653`*^9, 3.9792922857980747`*^9}, {3.979292341083699*^9, 
   3.979292345378234*^9}, {3.9792923794165373`*^9, 3.979292404346846*^9}, {
   3.979292443437128*^9, 3.9792925489681253`*^9}, 3.979293089384967*^9, {
   3.979293937924892*^9, 3.979294219525239*^9}, {3.979304505709181*^9, 
   3.979304506301462*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"811e68f6-cac6-405c-8e0b-\
9747122e9bb2"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Introduction: A Quest", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979251714184195*^9, 3.979251716835116*^9}, {
  3.9792887598867826`*^9, 
  3.9792887620315313`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"add37f9e-2eab-46a5-9d87-\
d65cdb289931"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Wizard, Chandra, reveals a quest: \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]find the \
blueprints, the keys that explain this ancient artifact I have, this wondrous \
machine, more wondrous than Antikythera, this interactive visualizer of \
orbits around a spinning black hole. Without the plans, I can\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t understand or explain these things that the machine does!\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] He shows us: ",
 StyleBox["The 3D Spirograph",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", wherein the orbits fly up and down, out of the plane, but never escape a \
donut-shaped envelope; ",
 StyleBox["The Hula Hoop",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", wherein the orbits become Schwarzschild\[LongDash]planar\[LongDash]when \
the black hole stops spinning; ",
 StyleBox["The Rip Tide",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", wherein particles dumped straight down into the black hole touch the \
Ergosphere and are swept sideways and flung away. \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Worse yet,\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] the wizard says, \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]I can\[CloseCurlyQuote]t replicate, maintain, or \
repair the machine. If it breaks, it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s lost forever!\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979218085032246*^9, 3.9792180872858*^9}, {
   3.97921812726119*^9, 3.9792182067340307`*^9}, {3.979249773235776*^9, 
   3.979249823287071*^9}, {3.979249862766975*^9, 3.979250047603253*^9}, {
   3.9792502260044813`*^9, 3.97925033483666*^9}, {3.979250553762299*^9, 
   3.979250737670985*^9}, {3.9792508280660973`*^9, 3.9792509785106277`*^9}, {
   3.97925133295507*^9, 3.979251466942944*^9}, {3.979251755065008*^9, 
   3.979251904427862*^9}, {3.979252237812505*^9, 3.979252241891869*^9}, {
   3.979286826465723*^9, 3.9792868405712023`*^9}, {3.979287277679369*^9, 
   3.979287367603675*^9}, {3.97928869667246*^9, 3.979289283877121*^9}, {
   3.979289316400536*^9, 3.979289361201816*^9}, {3.979289660777204*^9, 
   3.979289833523119*^9}, {3.97928986430659*^9, 3.97929003648954*^9}, {
   3.979290076268664*^9, 3.979290279347597*^9}, {3.979290351417584*^9, 
   3.97929037970683*^9}, {3.9792904347935953`*^9, 3.979290568197463*^9}, {
   3.979291350150494*^9, 3.9792914998855133`*^9}, {3.979294234305711*^9, 
   3.979294235277051*^9}, {3.979302396309739*^9, 3.9793024701762114`*^9}, {
   3.979303100138832*^9, 3.97930313053386*^9}, {3.979312366715281*^9, 
   3.979312373750779*^9}, 
   3.9793139080446367`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"44ebb89a-025c-4642-9f5a-\
9e8766bc8893"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The clockwork of the visualizer is an indecipherable bloc of definitions. \
Our quest is to explain them. To do that, we must find the keys that lie on \
the road. The wizard gives us a map, a linearized far-field approximation. \
But the wizard warns us that a dragon named ansatz Kerr stands in the way: \
the full vacuum field equations are too hard to look at, let alone to solve. \
But, the wizard gives us a formula and provisions\[LongDash]new compiler \
functions\[LongDash]for a magical sword, ",
 StyleBox["Ernst",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", that can help us. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979218085032246*^9, 3.9792180872858*^9}, {
   3.97921812726119*^9, 3.9792182067340307`*^9}, {3.979249773235776*^9, 
   3.979249823287071*^9}, {3.979249862766975*^9, 3.979250047603253*^9}, {
   3.9792502260044813`*^9, 3.97925033483666*^9}, {3.979250553762299*^9, 
   3.979250737670985*^9}, {3.9792508280660973`*^9, 3.9792509785106277`*^9}, {
   3.97925133295507*^9, 3.979251466942944*^9}, {3.979251755065008*^9, 
   3.979251904427862*^9}, {3.979252237812505*^9, 3.979252241891869*^9}, {
   3.979286826465723*^9, 3.9792868405712023`*^9}, {3.979287277679369*^9, 
   3.979287367603675*^9}, {3.97928869667246*^9, 3.979289283877121*^9}, {
   3.979289316400536*^9, 3.979289364614991*^9}, {3.979289400421259*^9, 
   3.979289421664435*^9}, {3.979289481025236*^9, 3.9792895179215384`*^9}, {
   3.979290592642396*^9, 3.9792906109368362`*^9}, {3.97929069837016*^9, 
   3.979290715259185*^9}, {3.979290779140274*^9, 3.979290989440477*^9}, {
   3.979291021851308*^9, 3.979291032008389*^9}, 3.979291159243382*^9, {
   3.9792926221770067`*^9, 3.979292697564884*^9}, {3.979294292295882*^9, 
   3.9792943114192*^9}, {3.97930456485845*^9, 
   3.9793046046111593`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5a276d62-d53b-4449-abc9-\
b8b3a4dffc48"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The Dragon",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": We write the Einstein vacuum field equations, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Ricci", "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "958a507b-94a8-4884-8016-b850a674bedb"],
 ", over an ansatz metric of four diagonal components, as we did with \
Schwarzschild, but this time including a fifth, coupling term, conjured \
intuitively, in the symmetrical ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"t", "\[LongDash]", "\[Phi]"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "aa579ff5-66a4-435a-a801-c5217afbfeca"],
 " slots. While the equations are easy for \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] \
to write, they are stupendously large, with 300-800 terms each. It is not \
feasible to see structure amongst the enormity, to see a starting point for \
teasing the equations apart and solving them incrementally. (TODO: perhaps AI \
can take a stab at solving them; I didn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t try it.)"
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979251007818901*^9, 3.979251320659028*^9}, {
  3.97925148152369*^9, 3.979251508366983*^9}, {3.979251923044775*^9, 
  3.9792519343597393`*^9}, {3.979252279203951*^9, 3.979252288972143*^9}, {
  3.979287426778748*^9, 3.979287517836838*^9}, {3.979291065028103*^9, 
  3.979291099673541*^9}, {3.979292730205348*^9, 3.979292731034466*^9}, {
  3.97929434331606*^9, 3.979294364058465*^9}, {3.97931246130066*^9, 
  3.979312461517189*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4323d688-c089-4906-af46-\
ac307b86e24a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The Wizard\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Map",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": Are we on the right road? A simplified, linearized, weak-field, far-field \
ansatz that looks like Newton-Kepler with frame-dragging shows that, yes, we \
are on the right road, the keys lie beyond the dragon. But we can\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t slay him, and we can\[CloseCurlyQuote]t step around him \
because he is surrounded by an impenetrable thicket of thorny algebra."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97925152622043*^9, 3.979251620867999*^9}, {
   3.979252296929006*^9, 3.979252333433988*^9}, {3.979288131337208*^9, 
   3.979288134935541*^9}, 3.97929113777874*^9, {3.979294396581807*^9, 
   3.979294413848153*^9}, {3.9793046453397627`*^9, 
   3.979304692935264*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bc872cd8-0dfa-4b41-a534-\
1a8541df9a75"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The Magical Sword",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": a sword name ",
 StyleBox["Ernst",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " can help us. If we can find pieces of a jewel in the thicket blocking the \
road, we can slot them into the hilt of the sword and enchant the monster \
into letting us pass. Ernst gives us a simplified equation that the Kerr \
metric must satisfy. We write the equation in \[ScriptCapitalU]\
\[ScriptCapitalD] and recapitulate his proof. "
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9792516385762997`*^9, 3.979251687025613*^9}, {
  3.9792519796903677`*^9, 3.979252008030642*^9}, {3.979291178121875*^9, 
  3.979291221022523*^9}, {3.9793044070414133`*^9, 3.979304470588736*^9}, {
  3.97930469929694*^9, 3.979304699673975*^9}, {3.979305540021379*^9, 
  3.979305615386142*^9}, {3.9793126213875637`*^9, 
  3.9793126276288757`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1942e9f8-644a-4383-9f81-\
74a98d4f37bb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The Road Beyond",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": We compare our metric to the Wolfram Function Repository (WFR) and find a \
match."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979252029129222*^9, 3.979252101520535*^9}, {
  3.979294430318396*^9, 
  3.9792944305030003`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"40c3728d-3214-4fc7-b891-\
57d99e3ea25b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The Quest Achieved",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": We find the vacuum equations now tractable, symbolically and numerically, \
and show how to build them into the visualizer. We now can explain, in \
detail, The 3D Spirograph, The Hula Hoop, The Rip Tide. "
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979252107590763*^9, 3.979252160777254*^9}, {
  3.979252364254335*^9, 3.9792524202055283`*^9}, {3.979291235816399*^9, 
  3.9792912901940403`*^9}, {3.979291323345975*^9, 
  3.979291335583846*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"39be23d5-fa6e-4e6e-af75-\
466424bfbefc"],

Cell["\<\
Along the way, the toolkit is subjected to torture test and found worthy.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979218085032246*^9, 3.9792180872858*^9}, {
   3.97921812726119*^9, 3.9792182067340307`*^9}, {3.979249773235776*^9, 
   3.979249823287071*^9}, 3.979249862766975*^9, {3.979252206901249*^9, 
   3.979252222904436*^9}, {3.979252440403129*^9, 3.979252452871101*^9}, {
   3.979252654675126*^9, 3.979252657470542*^9}, {3.979287608421877*^9, 
   3.979287622767536*^9}, {3.9793047925979767`*^9, 
   3.9793047947134943`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5bbedb63-e3b3-4687-aa19-\
60b133b5c5cf"],

Cell["\<\
Before we set out, the wizard fully provisions us for the quest.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979304799181602*^9, 3.979304811369163*^9}, {
  3.979305474341236*^9, 
  3.97930547529493*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ae4f5af6-cba7-45b6-aa4d-\
1fe02b5dc9a9"]
}, Open  ]],

