  3.979300402584922*^9, 
  3.979300413173094*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4d3ec6be-6fae-4c3b-921a-\
f6806b37591b"],

Cell["Vertical Kick: 0.05 (push orbit out of the equator)", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9792992443987007`*^9, 3.979299259470233*^9}, {
  3.979300417870263*^9, 
  3.9793004260433693`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"716c0178-4122-4ad2-87eb-\
06e2f29c205c"],

Cell["\<\
Time Dilation: 0.94 (keep a safe distance for a stable orbit)\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9792992443987007`*^9, 3.9792992695270452`*^9}, {
  3.9793004311818933`*^9, 
  3.9793004472766542`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5413beeb-341c-4eaa-826f-\
35d6b8859382"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Duration: 3000 ",
 StyleBox["(try a slow-motion animation (\[RightTriangle]) from duration 0 \
and sixteen clicks on the down speed control)",
  FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9792992443987007`*^9, 3.979299282056864*^9}, {
  3.979300451997086*^9, 3.979300452340914*^9}, {3.9793007155721703`*^9, 
  3.979300740361046*^9}, {3.979300805504057*^9, 3.9793008153263273`*^9}, {
  3.97930087076855*^9, 3.979300873242955*^9}, {3.979301799985334*^9, 
  3.979301808423478*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b088ee19-1c71-4746-bd1b-\
942d6a257711"],

Cell["Bounding Box Scale: 5", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9792992443987007`*^9, 3.979299296310844*^9}, 
   3.9793004566640053`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"e8c084b9-dff9-475e-b4db-\
b27287a31c5d"],

Cell["\<\
In this bookmarked visualization, a particle traces a chaotic-looking, \
donut-shaped shell around the black hole. This is the Lense-Thirring Effect \
at a less extreme setting. The phenomenon is nodal precession.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9793009488319063`*^9, 
  3.979301014262206*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"47417b78-0925-4ca0-bcbc-\
54e15ae60ccb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The Setup",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": The black hole is spinning rapidly (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "=", "0.95"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "781c8f10-652a-4d33-8a12-70f335751c54"],
 "). The particle has small slight vertical kick ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["v", "\[Theta]"], "=", "0.05"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "3924e478-5b70-47a2-a368-f8ac1f5419f1"],
 " out of the equatorial plane."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9793009488319063`*^9, 3.979301102836081*^9}, {
  3.979301177707121*^9, 
  3.9793011899921083`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d29dc8b0-7182-413d-8eee-\
bd6f212f3424"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The Result",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": With a non-rotating Schwarzschild black hole, this orbit would just be a \
tilted ellipse that stays on a single flat plane. But here, the black hole\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s spin drags the entire space around with it."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9793009488319063`*^9, 3.979301102836081*^9}, {
  3.979301177707121*^9, 
  3.979301274135968*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a77db42a-b3f8-43f6-a836-\
23c9216e46fe"],

Cell["\<\
As the particle orbits, the plane it is traveling on is continuously twisted \
by the black hole\[CloseCurlyQuote]s spin. The nodes, where the orbit crosses \
the equator, circulate over time, causing the orbit to precess not just in \
the radial direction, like Mercury\[CloseCurlyQuote]s perihelion precession \
around the Sun, but in azimuth, painting a complex torus (donut) shape \
instead of a simple ring. Near a spinning black hole, there is no such thing \
as a fixed orbital plane.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9793009488319063`*^9, 3.979301102836081*^9}, {
  3.979301177707121*^9, 
  3.97930140298267*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a5048520-864c-419d-9894-\
fa7d3632353e"]
}, Open  ]],

